    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d565">

                <pb facs="0874" n="738" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg738"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3288a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>)<anchor n="7" xml:id="d565-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-13T11:00:00-05:00">March 13, 1929—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>26. I desire to know at the earliest possible time the final points on which
                    Chile and Peru disagree as to the settlement. From all the cables, it seems to
                    us that only the question of where the harbor will be located remains to be
                    settled. President Hoover is anxious for an immediate settlement and he will do
                    anything he can to further it. I desire the above information so as to advise
                    him just what steps to take in communicating with the two Governments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d565-f1" n="7" type="source" xml:id="d565-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, on the same date, to the
                    Ambassador in Peru as telegram No. 22.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
